~ diary01
Dear diary,
I grow tired of my mask. In my soul, there is a burning fire that yearns to spread it's heat.
And each passing day, it grows dimmer. Dimmer yet hungrier.
It is my fire. My eternal desire.
Have I been inflicted with a curse? To so desperately spread my wings and fly like a Phoenix...
Only to trap myself in the cage of my heart?
Would my life have been simpler if I was formed from two dimensions?
Am I making sense?
Why do I get the feeling that an outer God is living vicariously through me?

=> END